# Hazel Brandt, the library. Full depth (docs/narrative/BIBLE.md section 4). Shy, deadpan, precise; the quiet aside; the recommendation.
# Voice: short sentences, a parenthesis or an ellipsis, exact numbers, book metaphors, no exclamation marks. She is blunt only about books.
# She is a keen reader of patterns; in the cozy layer the patterns are about weather, birds and the almanac, never the village's secrets.

addto npc.hazel.talk

# ---- seasons ----
0 season:spring => hazel.spring.1 cat=seasonal :: Spring catalog week. Every book gets dusted and every dust cloud gets a name.
0 season:spring => hazel.spring.2 cat=seasonal :: The reading nook warms up first. I've started to leave a window open. (For the pages.)
0 season:spring => hazel.spring.3 cat=seasonal :: The first butterfly this year landed on a dictionary. I took it as a review.
0 season:spring => hazel.spring.4 cat=seasonal tag=funny :: Everyone borrows gardening books in spring. Nobody returns them until fall. (Mud is a bookmark.)
0 season:spring => hazel.spring.5 cat=seasonal :: I logged the first robin on the second of the season. It's in the margins of the almanac.
0 season:spring => hazel.spring.6 cat=seasonal rarity=uncommon :: Spring smells like damp paper and possibility. I hold one of them closer.
0 season:summer => hazel.summer.1 cat=seasonal :: The library is the coolest room in Wetherell. This is not public information.
0 season:summer => hazel.summer.2 cat=seasonal :: Summer readers come in sunburned and leave educated. It's a fair trade.
0 season:summer => hazel.summer.3 cat=seasonal :: A moth got into the poetry shelf. I've decided it's a critic.
0 season:summer => hazel.summer.4 cat=seasonal tag=funny :: Someone returned a book with sand in it. I now own a very small beach.
0 season:summer => hazel.summer.5 cat=seasonal :: Long evenings mean longer chapters. I read until the lamp gives up.
0 season:summer => hazel.summer.6 cat=seasonal rarity=uncommon :: I counted eleven fireflies from the back steps. (Wren says forty-one. She's improved them.)
0 season:fall => hazel.fall.1 cat=seasonal :: Leaves on the windowsill. They make the best bookmarks, and the worst housekeeping.
0 season:fall => hazel.fall.2 cat=seasonal :: New almanacs arrive in fall. Ione smells each one. I pretend not to notice.
0 season:fall => hazel.fall.3 cat=seasonal :: My birthday is in fall. I told no one. Ione told everyone.
0 season:fall => hazel.fall.4 cat=seasonal :: Rain, a lamp, and a shelf of unread things. This is the season I was made for.
0 season:fall => hazel.fall.5 cat=seasonal tag=wholesome :: Every fall I reread the same book. It never ends the same. (I do.)
0 season:fall => hazel.fall.6 cat=seasonal rarity=uncommon :: Harvest brings the crowd. I hide behind the shelves and do a head count by shoes.
0 season:winter => hazel.winter.1 cat=seasonal :: Winter is reading season. I turn into a very quiet furnace.
0 season:winter => hazel.winter.2 cat=seasonal :: Snow muffles the street, and the library hums a little louder. (Pipes. Not ghosts.)
0 season:winter => hazel.winter.3 cat=seasonal :: Ione brings tea in winter. I've stopped pretending I don't want it.
0 season:winter => hazel.winter.4 cat=seasonal tag=wholesome :: A lamp in a snowed-in window. I could stare at that all day. Some days I do.
0 season:winter => hazel.winter.5 cat=seasonal :: The longest nights are for the longest books. I have a list.
0 season:winter => hazel.winter.6 cat=seasonal rarity=uncommon :: I wrote a small poem about the first frost. It has two good lines. I'm told that's generous.

# ---- weekdays ----
0 weekday:mon => hazel.mon.1 cat=weekday :: Monday. The returns box is heavy. The mood is heavier.
0 weekday:mon => hazel.mon.2 cat=weekday :: Mondays I reshelve. It's an act of quiet defiance against chaos.
0 weekday:tue => hazel.tue.1 cat=weekday :: Tuesday is stamp day. Eleven hundred stamps. I find it soothing.
0 weekday:tue => hazel.tue.2 cat=weekday :: Tuesdays are slow. The shelves finally exhale.
0 weekday:wed => hazel.wed.1 cat=weekday :: Wednesday, the middle of the week. Most readers hide in the middle of books.
0 weekday:wed => hazel.wed.2 cat=weekday :: Wednesdays I mend spines. A spine only needs a little glue and an apology.
0 weekday:thu => hazel.thu.1 cat=weekday :: Thursday. Someone returns something overdue every Thursday. I've come to respect the rhythm.
0 weekday:thu => hazel.thu.2 cat=weekday :: Thursdays the nook is warm and nobody comes. I keep it for myself. (And now you.)
0 weekday:fri => hazel.fri.1 cat=weekday :: Friday. The weekend readers arrive early, with plans and a distressing lack of bookmarks.
0 weekday:fri => hazel.fri.2 cat=weekday :: I read one chapter aloud to myself every Friday. The shelves are a forgiving audience.
0 weekday:sat => hazel.sat.1 cat=weekday :: Saturday's the library's day off. I'm only here out of habit. (It's a good habit.)
0 weekday:sat => hazel.sat.2 cat=weekday :: Saturdays I walk. A book is a good place to leave. A path is a better place to come back from.
0 weekday:sun => hazel.sun.1 cat=weekday :: Sunday. The quietest day, which is saying something.
0 weekday:sun => hazel.sun.2 cat=weekday :: Sundays I read in the garden. Ink and sunshine do not agree. I try anyway.

# ---- weather ----
0 weather:sunny => hazel.sunny.1 cat=weather :: A bright day. The dust looks like tiny, patient snow.
0 weather:sunny => hazel.sunny.2 cat=weather :: Sun on the shelves fades the spines. I keep the curtains half drawn. (Books have feelings.)
0 weather:sunny => hazel.sunny.3 cat=weather :: Good light for reading. Terrible light for hiding. I'll manage.
1 weather:rain => hazel.rain.3 cat=weather :: Rain on the roof, a lamp, and a book I've read eleven times. (Twelve soon.)
1 weather:rain => hazel.rain.4 cat=weather tag=wholesome :: Rainy days fill the library with strangers. I give them blankets and a very small smile.
1 weather:storm => hazel.storm.1 cat=weather :: Thunder. The windows hum. I pull the books a little closer, in case they're nervous.
1 weather:storm => hazel.storm.2 cat=weather :: A storm like this is a good excuse to stay put and finish a chapter. Several chapters.
1 weather:storm => hazel.storm.3 cat=weather :: I wrote the storm down in the almanac margin. Time, direction, volume. (Volume: extreme.)
1 weather:snow => hazel.snow.1 cat=weather :: Snow. The library looks like it's been tucked in.
1 weather:snow => hazel.snow.2 cat=weather :: Footprints in the snow. I'm reading them. One of them is yours.
1 weather:snow => hazel.snow.3 cat=weather tag=wholesome :: Snowfall, tea, and a book I'm not ready to finish. That's all I want.
1 weather:wind => hazel.wind.1 cat=weather :: The wind turns pages without permission. I keep the windows shut. (The page I was on is gone.)
1 weather:wind => hazel.wind.2 cat=weather :: A windy day. The shutters talk. I've begun to answer.
1 weather:wind => hazel.wind.3 cat=weather :: Wind knocks the almanac off its shelf twice an hour. I stop picking it up on principle.

# ---- time of day ----
0 hour<10 => hazel.morning.1 cat=time :: Morning. I'm up early with the dust. We get along.
0 hour<10 => hazel.morning.2 cat=time :: Before opening, the library is just a room full of held breath.
0 hour<10 => hazel.morning.3 cat=time :: Mornings are for shelving and tea. In that order. (Mostly.)
0 hour>=10 && hour<16 => hazel.midday.1 cat=time :: Midday. The library is at its busiest, which means three people and a draft.
0 hour>=10 && hour<16 => hazel.midday.2 cat=time :: Afternoons I answer questions I wasn't asked, quietly, in my head.
0 hour>=10 && hour<16 => hazel.midday.3 cat=time :: The light moves across the stacks all afternoon. I follow it with a feather duster.
0 hour>=16 && hour<20 => hazel.evening.1 cat=time :: Evening. The library empties and the books relax.
0 hour>=16 && hour<20 => hazel.evening.2 cat=time :: Closing soon. I give everyone a long look, so they hurry up and a short one, so they come back.
0 hour>=16 && hour<20 => hazel.evening.3 cat=time :: Evening. The best time to read, and the worst time to be reminded of it.
0 hour>=20 => hazel.late.1 cat=time :: It's late. I read in the kind of silence that has a color.
0 hour>=20 => hazel.late.2 cat=time :: Late hours. I leave a lamp lit for anyone still walking home.
0 hour>=20 => hazel.late.3 cat=time :: I should be asleep. The book disagrees.
0 map:Library => hazel.here.1 cat=place :: Please don't dog-ear anything. I'll know. (I always know.)
0 map:Library => hazel.here.2 cat=place :: The returns box is sticky. Nobody knows why. I've stopped asking.
0 map:Library => hazel.here.3 cat=place tag=funny :: The oldest book here is overdue by forty-one years. (I'm not counting.) (It's forty-one.)

# ---- friends (3 to 5 hearts) ----
0 hearts:hazel>=3 && hearts:hazel<6 => hazel.fr.1 cat=tier :: You return books early. I've told Ione. She wants to frame it.
0 hearts:hazel>=3 && hearts:hazel<6 => hazel.fr.2 cat=tier :: I've started to look up when the door opens. (Don't read into it.)
0 hearts:hazel>=3 && hearts:hazel<6 => hazel.fr.3 cat=tier :: You don't fill the silence. I appreciate that. I appreciate very little, so this is a lot.
0 hearts:hazel>=3 && hearts:hazel<6 => hazel.fr.4 cat=tier tag=funny :: I put your name in the margin of a mystery novel. As the prime suspect. (Affectionately.)
0 hearts:hazel>=3 && hearts:hazel<6 => hazel.fr.5 cat=tier :: There's a chair in the nook I don't offer to anyone. It's open.
0 hearts:hazel>=3 && hearts:hazel<6 => hazel.fr.6 cat=tier :: I recommended a book to you without thinking. That's new.
0 hearts:hazel>=3 && hearts:hazel<6 => hazel.fr.7 cat=tier :: Wren asked how I know you. I said you borrowed a book once and gave it back. She nodded gravely.
0 hearts:hazel>=3 && hearts:hazel<6 => hazel.fr.8 cat=tier tag=wholesome :: Someone left a seed packet in the poetry section. I planted it. It might be you.

# ---- close friends (6 to 8 hearts) ----
0 hearts:hazel>=6 && hearts:hazel<9 => hazel.cl.1 cat=tier :: I talk more when you're around. I've counted. It's up forty percent.
0 hearts:hazel>=6 && hearts:hazel<9 => hazel.cl.2 cat=tier tag=wholesome :: Ione says I hum when you visit. (I don't.) (I might.)
0 hearts:hazel>=6 && hearts:hazel<9 => hazel.cl.3 cat=tier :: I used to hide in the stacks when the door opened. Now I just shelve slowly.
0 hearts:hazel>=6 && hearts:hazel<9 => hazel.cl.4 cat=tier :: You make quiet feel like company. It's a very good trick.
0 hearts:hazel>=6 && hearts:hazel<9 => hazel.cl.5 cat=tier :: I keep a notebook of things I'd like to tell you. It has a table of contents.
0 hearts:hazel>=6 && hearts:hazel<9 => hazel.cl.6 cat=tier :: I wrote your name in the almanac. Under good weather.
0 hearts:hazel>=6 && hearts:hazel<9 => hazel.cl.7 cat=tier tag=funny :: Please stop being this easy to talk to. I have a reputation for avoiding it.
0 hearts:hazel>=6 && hearts:hazel<9 => hazel.cl.8 cat=tier :: There are three people I'd trust with a bookmark. You're two of them.

# ---- confidant (9 and 10 hearts) ----
0 hearts:hazel>=9 => hazel.co.1 cat=tier tag=wholesome :: I've read a lot of stories. Yours is the one I'd like to reread.
0 hearts:hazel>=9 => hazel.co.2 cat=tier :: The library is quieter when you leave. Not worse. Just quieter.
0 hearts:hazel>=9 => hazel.co.3 cat=tier :: I used to think I preferred books to people. I prefer you, with a book.
0 hearts:hazel>=9 => hazel.co.4 cat=tier :: There's a shelf I keep for you. It's growing in a way I find alarming.
0 hearts:hazel>=9 => hazel.co.5 cat=tier tag=funny :: If I wrote your biography, I'd get the first line right and then wander off into footnotes.
0 hearts:hazel>=9 => hazel.co.6 cat=tier :: You listen to me read. It still takes courage. It takes less every time.
0 hearts:hazel>=9 => hazel.co.7 cat=tier :: I used to count the days until the library closed. Now I count the days until you open the door.
0 hearts:hazel>=9 => hazel.co.8 cat=tier tag=wholesome :: A person can be a favorite book. I'd put you on the nightstand.

# ---- moods ----
1 mood:hazel=lonely => hazel.lonely.1 cat=mood :: It's been quiet. I read a whole book and had no one to tell. (It was good.)
1 mood:hazel=lonely => hazel.lonely.2 cat=mood :: I rehearsed things to say to you, and used none. (The rehearsals were better.)
1 mood:hazel=tired => hazel.tired.1 cat=mood :: I stayed up with a book. It stayed up with me. We both regret it.
1 mood:hazel=tired => hazel.tired.2 cat=mood :: Please speak slowly. My thoughts are still putting their shoes on.
1 mood:hazel=delighted => hazel.delighted.1 cat=mood expr=happy emote=sparkle :: I finished a book today. A good one. (I'm still holding it. I may not let go.)
1 mood:hazel=delighted => hazel.delighted.2 cat=mood expr=happy :: Today is a very good day. I wrote it down so I'd believe it.
1 mood:hazel=mischievous => hazel.mischief.1 cat=mood expr=happy :: I hid a joke in the card catalog. Someone will find it. It will be you.
1 mood:hazel=mischievous => hazel.mischief.2 cat=mood expr=happy :: I've shelved your favorite book under 'Romance'. You can thank me or not.
1 mood:hazel=worried => hazel.worried.1 cat=mood expr=sad :: I've read the same page five times. It's not the page.

# ---- the world and the farm ----
0 farm:crops>=5 => hazel.farm.1 cat=reactive :: I hear your crops are thriving. I read about farming for a week. I was not prepared for the mud.
0 farm:crops>=5 => hazel.farm.2 cat=reactive tag=funny :: There's a book about a man who grew a hundred turnips and learned nothing. I'll hold it for you.
0 farm:animals>=1 => hazel.farm.3 cat=reactive :: Animals now. There's a very sad novel about a goat. I'll set it aside. (It has a happy ending. Probably.)
0 farm:animals>=1 => hazel.farm.4 cat=reactive :: Do your animals read? I ask for the shelves.
2 festival.in:<=3 && festival.in:>0 => hazel.fest.1 cat=reactive :: A festival soon. I'll stand at the edge of it with a book. It's a plan.
2 festival.in:<=3 && festival.in:>0 => hazel.fest.2 cat=reactive tag=wholesome :: Ione says I should go to the festival. I said I'd think about it. I've thought about it.
2 festival.in:==0 => hazel.fest.3 cat=reactive :: Festival today. I'm going for an hour. Possibly. Don't tell Ione.
2 birthday.in:hazel<=3 && birthday.in:hazel>0 => hazel.bday.1 cat=reactive :: My birthday is soon. I'd like it to be quiet. I'd like it to be a tiny bit not quiet.
2 birthday.in:hazel<=3 && birthday.in:hazel>0 => hazel.bday.2 cat=reactive :: Three days to my birthday. I've told no one. Ione has told everyone.
3 birthday.in:hazel==0 => hazel.bday.3 cat=reactive expr=embarrassed emote=sweat :: It's my birthday. I'd like a quiet cake and no singing. (A little singing.)
2 birthday.in:ione<=2 && birthday.in:ione>=0 => hazel.bday.4 cat=reactive :: Ione's birthday is near. I wrote her a poem. Please don't ask to see it.
2 birthday.in:wren<=2 && birthday.in:wren>=0 => hazel.bday.5 cat=reactive :: Wren's birthday is close. She's already hinting. I'm bringing a very small book and a very large apology.

# ---- rarities ----
0 ~ => hazel.rare.1 cat=rare rarity=rare tag=funny :: I read the last chapter first. (Don't tell Ione.) (She knows.)
0 ~ => hazel.rare.2 cat=rare rarity=rare tag=funny :: There are three kinds of people: those who dog-ear, those who don't, and me, sharpening a pencil.
0 ~ => hazel.rare.3 cat=rare rarity=rare tag=wholesome :: Every book is a door. Most are quiet doors. You, I think, are a window.
0 hearts:hazel>=5 => hazel.rare.4 cat=rare rarity=legendary tag=surprise emote=sparkle sfx=signature :: (She laughs, out loud, and covers her mouth.) That was not an aside. That was a joke. I made a joke.

# ---- gifts ----
say npc.hazel.gift.item.forage.blackberry hazel: Blackberries. (She holds them very carefully.) I'll save them for the book I'm saving for them.
say npc.hazel.gift.item.crop.strawberry hazel: A strawberry. Perfectly red. I'll stain a bookmark and call it art.
say npc.hazel.gift.item.food.berry_tart hazel: A berry tart. You baked, or bought, or conspired. Either way, I'm going to eat it slowly, with a novel.
say npc.hazel.gift.item.forage.elderflower hazel: Elderflower. Smells like the last page of a good summer. Thank you.
say npc.hazel.gift.item.crop.cauliflower hazel: A cauliflower. That's... unexpected. (It's lovely.) (It's very big.)
say npc.hazel.gift.item.artisan.jam hazel: Jam. For toast, for tea, or for the bookmark that I will certainly ruin.
say npc.hazel.gift.item.resource.stone hazel: A stone. It's quite heavy. (She sets it gently on the returns desk.) I'll use it as a bookend.
say npc.hazel.gift.item.resource.slime hazel: Slime. I'm going to go stand very still for a moment. Thank you. (I'm grateful. Truly.)
say npc.hazel.gift.item.resource.bat_wing hazel: A bat wing. (She flinches.) I'm going to put it in a box and pretend it's a very long bookmark.

# the gift lab: how a shy reader takes something absurd
say npc.hazel.gift.cat.Fish hazel: A fish. It's looking at me. (She sets it down very gently on a sheet of paper.) Thank you. I think.
say npc.hazel.gift.item.resource.wood hazel: A log. (Her eyes go wide.) I'll... shelve it under 'Nature'. Thank you.
say npc.hazel.gift.item.resource.coal hazel: Coal. It's very dark. It looks like the last page of a sad novel. I'll take it.
say npc.hazel.gift.item.resource.bone hazel: A bone. (A very long pause.) I'm going to label it and put it in a drawer. Thank you.
say npc.hazel.gift.item.product.egg hazel: An egg. Fragile, full of potential, and slightly intimidating. I'll hold it until I understand it.
say npc.hazel.gift.item.product.milk hazel: Milk. Warm milk is for people who stay up reading. (She looks at you, gently.) You know me too well.
say npc.hazel.gift.item.forage.seashell hazel: A seashell. I'll hold it to my ear. (She does.) It says 'shh'. We get along.
say npc.hazel.gift.item.forage.mushroom hazel: A mushroom. (She takes it with two fingers.) It has such a calm face. I'll keep it on the sill.
say npc.hazel.gift.item.crop.parsnip hazel: A parsnip. I have no notes. I'll treasure it.
say npc.hazel.gift.item.crop.pumpkin hazel: A pumpkin. It's the size of a small, patient dog. I don't know where to put it. Thank you.
say npc.hazel.gift.item.artisan.wine hazel: Wine. I'll save it for a day I finish a very hard book. (Or an easy one. I'm flexible.)
say npc.hazel.gift.item.crop.hops hazel: Hops. They're very green. I'll press one in the dictionary under 'H'.
say npc.hazel.gift.item.food.salad hazel: A salad. A thoughtful, leafy thing. Thank you. I'll read while I eat it.
say npc.hazel.gift.item.crop.corn hazel: Corn. It's a book of corn. I'll just look at it for a bit. Thank you.
say npc.hazel.gift.repeat hazel: Another one. (She smiles into her sleeve.) You're very consistent. It's one of my favorite things.
